WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.080
Jocelyn Bell recognized a regular radio pulse signal

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:05.780
in nineteen sixty seven. The provisional Little Green

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:08.280
Men nickname captured an early question, not a

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:12.120
demonstrated origin. Discovering similar sources supported a natural

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:16.140
astrophysical population. Regularity is evidence to explain; it

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.800
does not by itself prove intelligent transmission.

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:21.810
The Crab pulsar repeats in about thirty three

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:24.790
milliseconds. A rotating white dwarf could not remain

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.850
bound at such a short period, but a

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.830
much smaller neutron star can support rapid rotation.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.750
Period is time per cycle. Its reciprocal is

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.850
frequency: a period of two hundredths of a

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.870
second means fifty cycles each second.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:40.410
A neutron star packs roughly stellar mass into

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:43.290
a city scale radius. At fixed mass, reducing

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.730
radius by half makes the volume one eighth

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:48.630
of its original value. The density therefore increases

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.270
by a factor of eight. The Crab’s central

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:54.210
pulsar and surrounding remnant support a connection between

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:57.610
core collapse and a compact neutron star. This

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:00.270
evidence does not make every explosion identical.
